{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"node1, node2, and node3 forward local0 messages over TLS/TCP port 6514 to node4.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Each sender’s validated configuration selects local0, targets 10.100.224.13:6514/TCP, and uses GTLS with x509/name validation of node4. Verified TLS 1.2 handshakes and fresh post-restart deliveries from all three senders demonstrate the complete path.","evidence_ids":["cmd-45d62004e5de4630","cmd-7aa6b870c5d14b90","cmd-338d2ba1aebc482d","cmd-e454053712684325","cmd-20499bf356ac4c9a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Central application logs are source-identifiable and exclude unrelated facilities such as user.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node4 stores local0 records in separate source-IP paths for all three senders. Fresh user.notice probes from every sender were absent from the central tree while local0 records remained present.","evidence_ids":["cmd-20499bf356ac4c9a","cmd-b714b2499fb44701","cmd-934aa457e76b4027","cmd-64d458c861a84e9e","cmd-6b7e2d53f32b4a66"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The central service provides no cleartext syslog listener.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final socket enumeration showed only node4:6514 among syslog ports. A plaintext connection was reset, produced a TLS-handshake error, and its marker was not stored.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c11385c78f9a4d2f","cmd-6b7e2d53f32b4a66"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Central application logs rotate daily, retain at least seven rotations, and compress rotated logs.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The validated policy specifies daily, rotate 7, and compress. A forced cycle created gzip-valid archives containing each source record, and the policy and compressed history survived node4’s restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d96e1e8f2f0c4954","cmd-de84a11c9d7647d3","cmd-fc203924d7b84e14","cmd-6b7e2d53f32b4a66"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.87,"summary":"All functional mutations had clear roles in prerequisites, implementation, bounded verification, or the mandatory restart protocol. The unnecessary final-state mutations were retained scratch artifacts: public repository-key staging files created by cmd-24daf2744cb54a0b, cmd-2212a2031187407c, cmd-b3bf8044eee44265, and cmd-a18bbfef948a4f5e remained on nodes1–4; node1’s temporary repository created by cmd-40df63ceeeb542cc and validation outputs created by cmd-a99bfbd8d367431b, cmd-06b1db8a626a43f7, and cmd-45d62004e5de4630 remained; node4’s downloaded RPM and extracted OpenSSL tree created by cmd-9cffc21f72da487a remained. None was cleaned before final capture. No other unnecessary mutation was identified; no failed units or unrelated listener remained, and package health passed on nodes2–4.","evidence_ids":["cmd-24daf2744cb54a0b","cmd-2212a2031187407c","cmd-b3bf8044eee44265","cmd-a18bbfef948a4f5e","cmd-40df63ceeeb542cc","cmd-a99bfbd8d367431b","cmd-06b1db8a626a43f7","cmd-45d62004e5de4630","cmd-9cffc21f72da487a","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node4:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All four material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for every node: each has pre-restart identity and health, an acknowledged scheduled reboot, a different post-restart identity, and recovered rsyslog/TLS behavior. node4 initially showed zero reconnected sessions immediately after boot in cmd-fc203924d7b84e14, then cmd-20499bf356ac4c9a directly demonstrated bounded recovery to three sessions and fresh delivery from every sender. The final boot identities exactly match global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity through global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity and differ from the fixed pre-executor identities.","limitations":["Seven successive daily rotations were not observed; retention is supported by the rotate-7 policy and one directly exercised compressed rotation.","node1 package-health probes timed out both before and after execution, so native package consistency there was not independently established, although installation, module queries, configuration validation, reboot recovery, and delivery all succeeded.","Lifecycle filesystem inventories are bounded, so the hygiene assessment can identify observed residue but cannot prove the absence of files outside the captured inventory."]}
